==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|mūlwurf}}, {{m|gmh|mūlwerf}}, which is composed of {{m|gmh|mūl|t=mouth}} (see {{m|de|Maul}}) and {{m|gmh|wurf|t=throwing}} (see {{m|de|werfen}}). 

This is a folk etymological reinterpretation of the earlier term {{m|gmh|moltwerf}}, from late {{der|de|goh|mul(t)wurf}}, which actually meant "earth(up)thrower," the first element from {{m|goh|molta|t=earth, dust}} (see {{m|de|Molte}}). Thus, the original word referred to the mole as a creature that throws up piles of earth. More at {{cog|en|mouldwarp}}.

